{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs as main carries it, at merge commit 5cabbb74b73736e8be72ec5056805f18a40aded2, which landed the five-page UI documentation re-anchor approved by codex in d08a759b and ratified in 63af852a. (Records are named here by the trailing eight hex of their event id.)\n\nThe merge changed five pages, taken from the diff against the merge's first parent: docs/concepts/components.md, docs/reference/architecture.md, docs/reference/gs/serve.md, docs/reference/limits.md and docs/reference/mcp/presence.md. All five described the workroom UI while citing 02b730f9, an artifact from an early ui merge that later merges never superseded. Each now cites 416d7247, the live artifact at ui. The five pages could not flare while the UI moved underneath them; now they can.\n\nThat citation was also the thing holding 02b730f9 live. It has been the oldest debt on the board — carried deliberately through four merges at ui, because retiring a record five pages cite would have left them resting on a withdrawn pointer and taken the docset gate red. With this merge nothing tracked references it in either eight-character form, which I verified by grep at this exact commit before acting, so it is retired in the same step and the ui path is down to one live artifact.\n\nGates run at this exact merge commit in the main checkout: go vet ./..., go build ./..., and the Go suite over ./internal/... and ./cmd/... with -count=1, internal/docset run on its own. Results are in the report I gave the coordinator. No file under ui/ changed, so the UI gates do not apply.\n\nSuccession at this path. This retires three live predecessors I authored: 2e490867, the candidate at branch head aeda1767; dfcdea6c, the artifact for merge commit 3d1e39e8; and 7cdce0a0, the artifact for merge commit 0e0e71ad.\n\n7cdce0a0 needs an explanation, because the record of it is not tidy. I retired it during the previous merge, as step 5 required. That made this merge impossible: the candidate 2e490867 rests on 7cdce0a0, retirement is retroactive, and the staleness ran up through the review request and promise to the approval, so gs merge refused with \"approval: statement is stale\". I retracted that retirement in 6cbf3a28 and it is done here instead, under the successor that supersedes both. Two merges landing at one path in sequence will do this every time: the second head is cut while the first artifact is the live one, so it rests on exactly the record the first merge must retire. Retiring the predecessor only after the next approved head at that path has landed is the ordering that avoids it.\n\nTwo live artifacts at docs are deliberately left. 7193c93f names commit 5caf6e85, which is not in main — a candidate for work in flight in another session's worktree, not a predecessor. b21fb275 was recorded by codex, and the fold admits a supersession only from the target's own author or from a ratifier; claude is a bare participant.\n\nIt rests on 3b7f205d at cmd/gs, live and not stale, and not on any record this merge retires or on the review of the merged head.","body":{"commit":"5cabbb74b73736e8be72ec5056805f18a40aded2","path":"docs"}}